{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>ויסעו [and they journeyed].</b> They had already journeyed from Rephidim, as I have shown you [there are] many like this:" "<b>ויחנו במדבר [and they encamped in the wilderness].</b> It is the wilderness of Sinai, [previously] mentioned:" "And the sense of ויחן שם ישראל [and Israel encamped there], after it said ויחנו במדבר [and they encamped in the wilderness], is that the heads of the tribes and the elders encamped opposite the mountain on account of their honor; therefore it mentioned ויחן [singular], for they were few. For according to their rank they stood on the day of the giving of the Torah around Mount Sinai, as I shall explain. And R. Solomon [Rashi] said that מנגד ההר [opposite the mountain] is east, and behold it is written מנגד סביב לאהל מועד יחנו (Numbers 2:2), which is from the four sides, for as the standards journey, so they encamp:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:47.704641139Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}